# Class: obo:FBbt_20000093 (adult antler neuron 029)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "FlyBase:FBrf0246888") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "FlyBase:FBrf0259490") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "FlyBase:FBrf0260535") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "FlyBase:FBrf0260546") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FBbt_20000093 "Adult brain-intrinsic neuron of the ATL029 group, with its soma in the brain, near to the antler (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It belongs to the DM1 antero dorsal hemilineage (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has postsynapses in the ipsilateral crepine, the ipsilateral lateral accessory lobe, the ipsilateral vest, the ipsilateral antler and the contralateral antler (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has presynapses in the ipsilateral antler, the contralateral antler, the ipsilateral crepine, the ipsilateral inferior bridge and the contralateral inferior bridge (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine (Eckstein et al., 2024). There are approximately 2 of these cells per organism (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024).")
