# Class: obo:FBbt_20002244 (adult saddle neuron 035)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "FlyBase:FBrf0246888") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "FlyBase:FBrf0259490") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "FlyBase:FBrf0260535") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "FlyBase:FBrf0260546") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FBbt_20002244 "Adult brain-intrinsic neuron of the SAD035 group, with its soma in the brain, lateral to the antennal lobe (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It belongs to the ALl1 ventral hemilineage (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has postsynapses in the ipsilateral anterior ventrolateral protocerebrum, the contralateral superior lateral protocerebrum, the ipsilateral superior lateral protocerebrum, the gnathal ganglia, the ipsilateral posterior ventrolateral protocerebrum, the contralateral superior clamp, the ipsilateral wedge and the saddle (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has presynapses in the contralateral superior lateral protocerebrum, the ipsilateral superior lateral protocerebrum, the contralateral superior clamp, the ipsilateral superior clamp and the contralateral mushroom body pedunculus (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine (Eckstein et al., 2024). There are approximately 2 of these cells per organism (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024).")
AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:FBbt_20002244 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705>)
AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:FBbt_20002244 "2020-07-30T12:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace obo:FBbt_20002244 "fly_anatomy.ontology")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:FBbt_20002244 "FBbt:20002244")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FBbt_20002244 "Uncharacterized putative cell type based on Hemibrain data (Scheffer et al., 2020) and updated using FlyWire (FAFB) data (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). Soma locations are based on the closest annotated neuropil region. Pre- or post-synapse locations are the fewest regions that collectively contain at least 80 percent of all pre- or post-synapses of these neurons in FlyWire. Neurotransmitter predictions are from Eckstein et al. (2024). Other annotations are based on annotations in FlyWire and are available in the supplemental material of Schlegel et al. (2024).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FBbt_20002244 "adult saddle neuron 035")
SubClassOf(obo:FBbt_20002244 obo:FBbt_00052046)
