# Class: obo:FBbt_20007304 (adult medulla visual centrifugal neuron 11)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "FlyBase:FBrf0259490") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "FlyBase:FBrf0260535") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "FlyBase:FBrf0260546") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FBbt_20007304 "Adult visual centrifugal neuron of the cM11 group, with its soma in the brain, posterior-dorsal to the inferior posterior slope (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It is a putative embryonic-born neuron (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has postsynapses in the ipsilateral anterior ventrolateral protocerebrum, the ipsilateral posterior lateral protocerebrum, the ipsilateral posterior ventrolateral protocerebrum, the ipsilateral inferior posterior slope and the ipsilateral medulla (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). It has presynapses in the ipsilateral medulla, the ipsilateral anterior ventrolateral protocerebrum, the ipsilateral wedge, the ipsilateral posterior lateral protocerebrum and the ipsilateral posterior ventrolateral protocerebrum (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine (Eckstein et al., 2024). There are approximately 2 of these cells per organism (Schlegel et al., 2024; Dorkenwald et al., 2024).")
AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:FBbt_20007304 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705>)
AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:FBbt_20007304 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5633-1314>)
AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:FBbt_20007304 "2024-02-05T12:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "FlyBase:FBrf0260535") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FBbt_20007304 "adult cM11 neuron")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace obo:FBbt_20007304 "fly_anatomy.ontology")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:FBbt_20007304 "FBbt:20007304")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FBbt_20007304 "Uncharacterized putative cell type from Schlegel et al. (2024), based on FlyWire v783 (FAFB) data (Dorkenwald et al., 2024; Schlegel et al., 2024). Soma locations are based on the closest annotated neuropil region. Pre- or post-synapse locations are the fewest regions that collectively contain at least 80 percent of all pre- or post-synapses of these neurons in FlyWire. Neurotransmitter predictions are from Eckstein et al. (2024). Other annotations are based on annotations in FlyWire and are available in the supplemental material of Schlegel et al. (2024).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FBbt_20007304 "adult medulla visual centrifugal neuron 11")
