# Class: obo:FBbt_20008042 (adult AN18B023 neuron)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "FlyBase:FBrf0259490") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "doi:10.7554/eLife.96084.1") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "doi:10.7554/eLife.97766.1") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "doi:10.7554/eLife.97769.1") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FBbt_20008042 "Adult ascending neuron of the AN18B023 group with bilateral VNC arbors (Takemura et al., 2024; Marin et al., 2024). It is a primary neuron of the 18B hemilineage (Takemura et al., 2024; Marin et al., 2024). It exits the VNC via the cervical connective (Takemura et al., 2024; Marin et al., 2024). It receives input in the T1 leg neuropil and neck neuropil and sends output to the neck neuropil (Takemura et al., 2024; Marin et al., 2024). Its predicted neurotransmitter is acetylcholine (Eckstein et al., 2024). There are approximately 2 of these cells per organism and their somas are found in the prothoracic neuromere (Takemura et al., 2024; Marin et al., 2024).")
